Description: Patina Desktop, a Wayland desktop environment written in Rust
 Patina is a Wayland compositor and desktop shell written in Rust. This
 pre-release provides the compositor (floating windows with titlebars drawn by
 the compositor, several displays, blur), the top panel, the dock, the lock
 screen (Ctrl+Alt+L, idle and before sleep) and a sign-in screen for greetd.
 It adds a "Patina" session to the login screen and a patina-session command
 for starting it from a text console.
 .
 Not yet included: launcher, notifications, quick settings, and the
 Terminal, File Bin and Settings apps. Until the Terminal app exists,
 install a Wayland terminal such as foot to have something to run.
 .
 Pick the session in GDM, SDDM or LightDM, use the included greetd sign-in
 screen (see /usr/share/doc/patina-desktop/greetd-config.toml), or run
 patina-session from a text console.
